nother 54\nok    HL1 the 325 basin layering (200 real lays) equals the old body, cold and after re-lays, and re-tests only changed pairs\n    HL2: 300 rebuilds equal (18 lays edited in place); ends on another 907, joiners over another 848; tested 4890, reused 38798\nok    HL2 fuzz: a long-lived layering cache equals the old body through lay swaps and width changes\nok    HL3 source: Layered passes its cache; FrameLegacy keeps the old body\n    HX1 200 strands, 153 with spans; CrossSpans 298 ms total (max 15.7), grid 318 ms (max 6.2; grids built per call)\nok    HX1 the 325 basin crossing spans (200 real strands) through the segment grids equal CrossSpans exactly\nok    HX2 fuzz: random strands (NaN, 0/1 points, huge segments, repeated points, reach above the grid's) equal CrossSpans\n    HX3 200 hoses, 40 relay frames (up to 24 strands re-posed a frame): old policy 2210 ms (max 79/frame), index 187 ms (max 10.1/frame); re-collections 4500 vs 8000; span builds 3048, marks 3884\nok    HX3 a relay wave on the basin strands: the index equals all-pairs every frame and re-checks only near strands\n    HX5 200 strands relaid at once, 8 scans a frame: drained in 26 frames, 2400 deferrals\nok    HX5 a budgeted wave: Pending tells Check's rescans exactly, and deferred strands converge to all-pairs\nok    HX4 source: the component feeds HoseCrossShadows off FrameLegacy and keeps the all-pairs body for FrameLegacy\nok    L1 HoseLayQueue: a landed, applied key asked again starts no lay (100 frames)\nok    L2 HoseLayQueue: 150 re-lays of 400 ms asked in one frame never cost an asking frame > 50 ms; budgets hold; all land\nok    L3 HoseLayQueue sync: 10 changed keys lay at most MaxStartsPerFrame a frame, all within 3 frames\nok    L4 HoseLayQueue: a key that moves mid-lay gets its landed lay under the OLD key, then exactly one job for the new key\nok    L5 HoseLayQueue: a lay that throws is a fault, not retried while its key holds; a new key is tried\nok    L6 HoseLayQueue.Compute on a CordWorld copy lays what the snapshot lays and leaves both untouched\nok    L7 RM_MapComponent_Hoses (source): DrawAll and the tick lay deferred, skipped under FrameLegacy; LayFrom is LayFromOn\nok    L8 HoseMath.RouteCells on three threads at once: each search counts (and caps) only its own expansions\nok    L9 HoseLayQueue: a job that lands after its reel's lay was reset (newer epoch) is dropped, released, and the current key started\nok    L10 HoseLayQueue: the in-flight cap holds across queues (maps, an abandoned game's queue)\nok    L11 epoch (source): every lay reset bumps layEpoch and the deferred ask passes it\nok    L12 counters (source): a worker's finally sets done, then drops AllInFlight before its queue's InFlight\nok    HoseReplan_R1 pending is never an answer: a running replan reads Pending, 'no route' only once landed\nok    HoseReplan_R2 the per-tick start quota is shared by every queue (two maps, 20 reels, one tick)\nok    HoseReplan_R3 a result that lands after the reel's lay epoch moved is dropped; the current replan starts\nok    HoseReplan_R4 a stale retract runs again, a stale keep applies, MaxStaleRetracts stale retracts are taken\nok    HoseReplan_R5 a replan that throws answers keep, never a retract, and keeps its text\nok    HoseReplan_R6 (source) the tick runs no CheckReplan: a cut asks the queue, pending is polled, blocks flow, is dropped\nok    HoseReplan_R7 the real CheckReplan through the queue: deferred is Pending, landed is 'no route'\nok    M1 HoseMateCache: a re-lay to the same shape (new list instances, 1e-4 jitter) re-solves nothing over 50 frames\nok    M2 HoseMateCache: an end that moves re-solves its pair exactly once; a changed lead-out counts as a move\nok    M3 HoseMateCache: six pairs changed at once cost at most one solve a frame and are all solved by frame 6\nok    M4 HoseMateCache async: a 400 ms solve never holds the asking frame past 50 ms; it lands on a later frame\nok    M5 HoseMateCache default solver = HoseSpliceMath.MatePair for the same inputs (90 degrees)\nok    M6 HoseMateCache async: a solve that throws surfaces as a fault on the main thread and is not retried\nok    M7 HoseMateCache async: an end that moves while its solve runs is never served the stale result\nok    ME1 HoseMateEndQueue async re-shape = direct HoseSpliceMath.MateEnd bit for bit (real pair, tail solve)\nok    ME2 HoseMateEndQueue latest wins: one job per reel, the older landed result handed out once, the newer key asked next\nok    ME3 HoseMateEndQueue budget: MaxStartsPerFrame starts a frame, MaxInFlight across frames, deferrals counted\nok    ME4 HoseMateEndQueue: a re-shape that throws lands as no re-shape (Error kept, Faulted counted), never escapes\n    RO1 random load: 8734 serves over 2000 frames, worst continuous wait 16 frames (N=50)\nok    RO1 HoseDrawRotation: reel order starves late reels under a full budget; rotation serves each within ceil(N/k) frames\nok    RO2 source: DrawAll walks a rotating start; budgets and the mate deferral record it; MateEnd off the frame\nok    LW1 a lay depends on the world's content only: fresh clone = reused pooled clone = rebuilt world (bit hash); TakeLayWorld uses World(LayWorldMaxAge)\nok    S1 Join: straight-on (heading east to a point ahead, curvature 0 both ends)\nok    S1 Join: 90 degrees, starting on a curve (k0 = 0.4) and ending straight\nok    S1 Join: U-turn (opposed headings, the end 1 cell to the side and behind)\nok    S1 Join: S offset with end curvature (k1 = -0.3)\nok    S2 the screenshot: B's end on A's end, both heading east, mates face to face\nok    S3 straight-on: B already arrives from the east heading west (near identity)\nok    S3 90 degrees: B comes down from the north onto A's end\nok    S3 opposed: B runs parallel beside A, same heading, ending one cell north of A's end\nok    S5 MatePair: at 90 degrees both hoses bend part way (gentler than one looping round); every case still passes the bars\n    splice cost: cold 18 ms (stiff); full search 71 solves, 687 iterations, 16.3 ms (not asserted)\nok    S4 a stiffer hose (MinBendRadius 2.0) keeps its bound; the screenshot solve is cheap\nok    HoseDraw_D1_a_bend_round_a_wall_end_never_shaves_its_corner\nok    HoseDraw_D2_a_port_met_from_the_side_draws_no_lead_in_stub\nok    HoseDraw_D3_a_side_arrival_at_a_moved_port_slides_onto_it\nok    HoseClothoid snap: Feasible only with both end headings within EndTol, ramp bound stretched as dk*sc\nok    HoseCurve_ruler_holds_its_floor_over_the_hard_stations (60/60, floor 60)\nok    HoseLayout_old_drawn_through_placements_now_refused_or_clear\nok    HoseLayout_too_close_to_bend_is_refused_with_the_player_reason\nok    HoseLayout_roomy_placements_still_lay_g2_and_clear\nok    WorldMapDrawGuard sees the hose and suspension draw updates (sanity probe)\nok    WorldMapDrawGuard every drawing MapComponentUpdate/OnGUI skips the world view\nok    HoseWall_S1_hose_on_a_seam_between_two_wall_cells_is_refused\nok    HoseWall_S2_corner_and_face_grazes_still_pass\nok    HoseWall_S3_WallDepth_agrees_with_the_independent_ruler\nok    HoseWall_S4_replanned_lays_never_cross_a_wall\nok    HoseBand_P5_refuses_a_dug_square_without_ramp_or_ladder\nok    HoseBand_P5_routes_lip_ramp_floor\nok    HoseBand_P5_routes_lip_ladder_floor_and_raised_ladder_leaves_it_hanging\nok    HoseBand_swim_split_pool_stays_one_floor\nok    Scenario_C4_C10_hoses_lay_offline\nok    HoseBand_P5_endpoint_reach_respects_band\nok    HoseBand_P5_newly_dug_square_replans_or_retracts_once\nok    HoseBand_P2_pit_cover_carries_no_hose\nok    HoseBand_P5_no_bands_leaves_gss_signatures_unchanged\nok    Suspension_tiers_are_the_items_numbers\nok    Suspension_drag_validator_ends_middle_length_width\nok    Suspension_islands_split_one_drag_into_bridges\nok    Suspension_spans_supports_and_swing_order\nok    Suspension_load_sag_and_falls\nok    Suspension_wiring_sources_defs_patches\nok    Islands_wiring_split_tower_cost_restore\nok    Grate_fire_attach_open_p